cff-version: "1.2.0"
message: "If you use this dataset or software, please cite this release."
title: "Indonesian-Javanese-English Sentiment Analysis with AutoML and XAI"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-03"
type: software
abstract: >-
  Corrected Python pipeline for three-class sentiment classification of
  Indonesian-Javanese-English code-mixed text. The pipeline compares FLAML,
  AutoGluon, and Optuna across three feature sets (TF-IDF, TF-IDF with
  code-mixing features, and TF-IDF with multilingual sentence embeddings),
  selects a configuration on development folds only, and explains the selected
  model with LIME. Every executing stage is gated by an approval file that
  binds a run to an exact protocol hash, code hash, and stage list. This
  release also carries the fixed dataset and its documented preprocessing.
authors:
  - family-names: "Hidayatullah"
    given-names: "Ahmad Fathan"
    affiliation: "Department of Informatics, Universitas Islam Indonesia"
repository-code: "https://github.com/fathanick/Indonesian-Javanese-English-Sentiment-Analysis-with-AutoML-and-XAI"
url: "https://github.com/fathanick/Indonesian-Javanese-English-Sentiment-Analysis-with-AutoML-and-XAI"
keywords:
  - sentiment analysis
  - code-mixed text
  - Indonesian
  - Javanese
  - English
  - AutoML
  - explainable artificial intelligence
  - LIME
  - natural language processing
